Z||000000||Dan87GT||05-08-2000||03:00 PM||||How do you change the ignition lock? My old one is shot(key pulls out when on). I have a new one but don't know the procedure. <BR>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||JohnnyK||05-08-2000||03:20 PM||||Wait a sec, I don't know if this is normal.. If my ignition is not turned back all the way, I can start it up without the key.. I can do everything so long as I don't hit that little lock and push the ignition back all the way.. Is this normal?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gold-86SE||05-08-2000||03:27 PM||||<BR>Dan,<BR>Sorry, if i knew how to replace the switch, the switch in my Sunbird would be done and then i could help you.<P>Johnny,<BR>I have a Sunbird with the same problem, and technically speaking, no this is not normal.<P>Your ignition switch is worn out, and should "technically" be replaced.  However, I have been driving my Sunbird with the ignition switch problem for about 2 1/2 years and so far nothing has happened (knock on wood).<P>The only real problem is that you have to notify those who may drive your fiero, that they cannot place the switch in the lock postion, but to leave the ignition in the off position.<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000003||TOM||05-08-2000||03:48 PM||||Pull the steering wheel pull thje lock plate pull the turn signal cam stuff then there is a screw that holds the cylinder in. You will need some special tools for the wheel and lockplate but they are cheap.||||reg||1
Z||000004||JohnnyK||05-09-2000||08:19 PM||||But this is soo useful... If I want safety, I just press the ignition lock thing... And if I don't, I can't think of anyone I know who would steal a Fiero!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
